WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.210
Here's how to bring a Steam Input layout from the Steam Workshop into PadForge.

2
00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.490
You're hearing a generated voice.

3
00:00:08.925 --> 00:00:13.075
First, open Settings, and tick Enable Community Configs.

4
00:00:13.585 --> 00:00:16.855
PadForge then contacts Steam's servers only when you search,

5
00:00:17.185 --> 00:00:19.495
open a config, or check for updates.

6
00:00:21.116 --> 00:00:25.866
On the Profiles page, click Browse Community Configs, and search for your game.

7
00:00:27.785 --> 00:00:29.995
Its configs are listed by rating.

8
00:00:30.505 --> 00:00:32.395
A chip narrows them to your controller.

9
00:00:32.945 --> 00:00:35.315
Open one to read its translation manifest.

10
00:00:37.195 --> 00:00:39.665
Clean rows carry over as they are.

11
00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:41.445
Partial ones work with a difference.

12
00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.785
Skipped ones are left out, and each row says why.

13
00:00:46.281 --> 00:00:47.711
Click Save Profile.

14
00:00:48.301 --> 00:00:53.031
The new profile has no controller yet, so assign yours, and link the game's program.

15
00:00:55.442 --> 00:00:57.952
Find more guides at padforge.org.
